[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=Lighting Preset ARAM v1.0\\Stores and recalls 16 analog values for||1
  Cmn2=6 lighting presets.\\The values live in this module. They are nonvolatile.
  Cmn3=\\\\Each preset N (1-6) is one group of three rows:\\  [D]PresetN_Recall||1
  Cmn4=||2panel Lighting.PresetNRecall (short press)\\  [D]PresetN_Save||1
  Cmn5=||4panel Lighting.PresetNSave (held the whole press)\\  [D]PresetN_FB||1
  Cmn6=||6panel Lighting.PresetN\\\\A blank row follows the six presets.
  Cmn7=||1Under that, set both\\analog arrays to the same size (16 to use||1
  Cmn8=every channel):\\  [A]Ain1-Ain16       live values to store and||1
  Cmn9=compare\\  [A]Aout1-Aout16     values driven on recall\\\\Only an||1
  Cmn10=Ain with a signal on it is stored, compared, or recalled.\\Ain and||1
  Cmn11=Aout on the same row cannot share one signal name.\\\\PresetN_Save||1
  Cmn12=is timed from its rising edge. Releasing it cancels\\whichever timer||1
  Cmn13=has not finished.\\  2.5 seconds   stores every defined Ain into||1
  Cmn14=preset N\\  10 seconds    erases preset N (stored values return||1
  Cmn15=to 0)\\\\PresetN_Recall copies that preset onto the defined Aout||1
  Cmn16=channels.\\An empty or erased preset does not drive the outputs.
  Cmn17=\\\\PresetN_FB is high only when that preset has been stored and\\
  Cmn18=every defined analog equals it. A defined analog is one with a\\
  Cmn19=signal on Ain or Aout. More than one preset may match.\\\\A recall||1
  Cmn20=makes those analogs the current values and checks\\immediately.||1
  Cmn21=Any later Ain change drops every PresetN_FB. After\\the inputs sit||1
  Cmn22=still for about 1 second, the check runs again.\\\\Erase, and a||1
  Cmn23=never-stored preset, stay dark. A look that was\\saved at zero still||1
  Cmn24=matches when the live values are zero.
[END]
